==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Funeral Storm Batter Haruhime''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Issun has a very low cooldown to compensate for his incomplete [[Weaken]] uptime, making him a decent crowd-controller for melee Angel enemies. While he isn't that bad, alternatives can often be chosen over him, such as [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] for her 100+% uptime and [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] for having a more potent ability on top of being able to gain Weaken through [[Talents]].

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Haruhime takes Issun and becomes a nuker-based attacker with unusually high range and a dash of crowd-control. For Haruhime's actual abilities, her [[Knockback]], while occasional, can help reposition many Angel enemy types as she outranges most of them, and her brief Weaken is only convenient at best. Her [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] only counters two Angel enemies; while [[Youcan]] was already easy to take care of, Wave Immunity helps against [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] and Knockback, with the support of Talented [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]], helps to keep his dangerous tirade from gaining distance.

Haruhime doesn't hold much weight as a generalist, however. [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] is oftentimes a better choice in spite of Haruhime's longer range, and many things about Haruhime can be called sluggish, from her speed down to her cooldown. Other preexisting anti-[[Wave Attack|Wave]] options, many no-gacha, already have little issue with Wave Attack enemies, so Haruhime hardly has anything to bring to the table. In general, she should just stick to being [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultima Galaxy Cosmo]]-like support while Fiend Cat and other similar Ubers do the heavy pushing.

